:answer/id #uuid "fd8d4981-cac9-569f-a5c8-dce13d00dbea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274617}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "31063f08-1e78-5379-8242-cacf1a1d6a7c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272824} :answer-field/id #uuid "c93918a5-c8b2-5c94-8ed4-2849b95cb1aa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274985}] :question/id #uuid "8f4ce117-1fd3-56dc-bc77-859fb08b2278" :question/math-academy-id "q-15304" :question/problem "A circle in the Cartesian plane is given by the equation $8x+{x}^{2}-2y=64-{y}^{2}.$ If the circle is written in the standard form $(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2},$ then $a+b+r=$" :question/worked-solution "To find the standard form of the circle, we need to group $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8x+{x}^{2}-2y & =64-{y}^{2} \\\\ ({x}^{2}+8x)+({y}^{2}-2y) & =64 \\\\ ({x}^{2}+2\\cdot 4x+{4}^{2})+({y}^{2}-2\\cdot y+{1}^{2}) & =64+{4}^{2}+{1}^{2} \\\\ ({x}^{2}+2\\cdot 4x+{4}^{2})+({y}^{2}-2\\cdot y+{1}^{2}) & =81\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can factor the perfect squares and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+4)^{2}+(y-1)^{2} & ={9}^{2} \\\\ (x-(-4))^{2}+(y-1)^{2} & ={9}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=-4,b=1$ and $r=9,$ and\n\n$$\na+b+r=-4+1+9=6.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275326 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e85bc55-e02c-54fc-8122-557e2841e870" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272659} {:answer/id #uuid "bdd36a44-0719-5e42-b8ba-c592a0f863c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274031} {:answer/id #uuid "cf716e16-5a7b-58d5-bd95-468707fb3db2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274193} {:answer/id #uuid "ee3f9ff3-e21e-5c4d-8faf-b3e8f4725