 :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "center: $(-1,1)$, radius: $9$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432231}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e0870e71-30f3-54e9-bb11-425115745529" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "center: $(1,0)$, radius: $9$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432230} :answer-field/id #uuid "475d7cd0-eeb5-57a4-b7c2-c1eef8977b26" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432237}] :question/id #uuid "3d51e7e2-42da-5029-94ba-a383fb96ca48" :question/math-academy-id "q-15466" :question/problem "Find the center and radius of the circle whose equation is ${x}^{2}-2x+{y}^{2}=80.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the center and radius of the circle, we need to group $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-2x+{y}^{2} & =80 \\\\ ({x}^{2}-2x)+{y}^{2} & =80 \\\\ ({x}^{2}-2\\cdot x+{1}^{2})+{y}^{2} & =80+{1}^{2} \\\\ ({x}^{2}-2\\cdot x+{1}^{2})+{y}^{2} & =81\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can factor the perfect squares and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-1)^{2}+{y}^{2} & ={9}^{2} \\\\ (x-1)^{2}+(y-0)^{2} & ={9}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the circle is centered at $(1,0)$ and its radius is $9.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186432245 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d6171a8-6197-560d-8edc-2b5e80c6ce81" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "center: $(6,8)$, radius: $11$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432200} {:answer/id #uuid "16f43589-ba4b-5fe3-b651-27dcee807b31" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "center: $(-12,-16)$, radius: $21$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432202} {:answer/id #uuid "9896f873-fcd7-5d43-8b83-249941df2b11" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "center: $(6,8)$, radius: $21$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432219} {:answer/id #uuid "cd5d7134-54b8-5fbc-9070-2f312605b654" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "ce