2186238036 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "546b362a-2747-5ca5-ab57-f8c2e8eaf565" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-2,1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236354} {:answer/id #uuid "92efcc88-d151-5156-8711-efffa00abe3d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-1,-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236750} {:answer/id #uuid "a24ccf86-225d-53ba-884b-3ce30a0309ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2,-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236835} {:answer/id #uuid "d5e0754e-5b71-56ae-8522-c2d740aa9e6b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-1,1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237169} {:answer/id #uuid "ef1e377a-ed1e-5800-9161-b7da79f63267" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237326}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "92efcc88-d151-5156-8711-efffa00abe3d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-1,-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236750} :answer-field/id #uuid "62416cbe-aee9-592b-877e-f41f242d04f0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237567}] :question/id #uuid "709039e0-3e6c-5c6c-99cd-c5947d7c381d" :question/math-academy-id "q-103668" :question/problem "Calculate the coordinates of the vertex of the parabola ${x}^{2}+2x-2y-1=0.$" :question/worked-solution "The standard equation of an upward- or downward-opening parabola that has its vertex at $(h,k)$ is\n\n$$\n(x-h)^{2}=4p(y-k),\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is constant.\n\nTo write the given equation in this form, we need to group the $x$-terms on the left-hand side and complete the square, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+2x-2y-1 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}+2x & =2y+1 \\\\ (x+1)^{2}-1 & =2y+1 \\\\ (x+1)^{2} & =2y+1+1 \\\\ (x+1)^{2} & =2y+2 \\\\ (x+1)^{2} & =4(\\frac{1}{2})(y+1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the vertex are $(h,k)=(-1,-1).$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253517