52-b279bf17bf67" :question/math-academy-id "q-11883" :question/problem "Calculate the coordinates of the vertex of the parabola $3{x}^{2}+6x+4y+15=0.$" :question/worked-solution "The standard equation of an upward- or downward-opening parabola that has its vertex at $(h,k)$ is\n\n$$\n(x-h)^{2}=4p(y-k),\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is constant.\n\nTo write the given equation in this form, we need to group the $x$-terms on the left-hand side and complete the square, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{2}+6x+4y+15 & =0 \\\\ 3{x}^{2}+6x & =-4y-15 \\\\ 3[{x}^{2}+2x] & =-4y-15 \\\\ 3[(x+1)^{2}-1] & =-4y-15 \\\\ 3(x+1)^{2}-3 & =-4y-15 \\\\ 3(x+1)^{2} & =-4y-15+3 \\\\ 3(x+1)^{2} & =-4y-12 \\\\ 3(x+1)^{2} & =-4(y+3) \\\\ (x+1)^{2} & =-\\frac{4}{3}(y+3) \\\\ (x+1)^{2} & =4(-\\frac{1}{3})(y+3)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the vertex are $(h,k)=(-1,-3).$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186238036 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "546b362a-2747-5ca5-ab57-f8c2e8eaf565" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-2,1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236354} {:answer/id #uuid "92efcc88-d151-5156-8711-efffa00abe3d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-1,-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236750} {:answer/id #uuid "a24ccf86-225d-53ba-884b-3ce30a0309ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2,-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236835} {:answer/id #uuid "d5e0754e-5b71-56ae-8522-c2d740aa9e6b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-1,1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237169} {:answer/id #uuid "ef1e377a-ed1e-5800-9161-b7da79f63267" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237326}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "92efcc88-d151-5156-8711-efffa00abe3d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-1,-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236750} :answer-field/id #uuid "62416cbe-aee9-592b-877e-f41f242d04f0" :answer-field/key "selection" :