s result back into our original expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-({x}^{2}+3x+3) & =-({(x+\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}+\\frac{3}{4}) \\\\  & =-{(x+\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}-\\frac{3}{4} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{4}-{(x+\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272062 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4ca67b8d-08c3-5756-8356-6307d581f0f1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{4}-{(x+\\frac{5}{2})}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269958} {:answer/id #uuid "68d03655-8b8a-586c-af0d-61d3ff3b9222" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{25}{4}-{(x+\\frac{5}{2})}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270198} {:answer/id #uuid "ac18e720-115f-5feb-9e45-b7fece57b20a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{4}-{(x+\\frac{5}{2})}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270804} {:answer/id #uuid "b09bfde5-2d06-51d1-ba5b-e32c34c0e17b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{53}{4}-{(x+10)}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270845} {:answer/id #uuid "df69391d-37bd-5f43-ba1f-a9d2a6f64153" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32-{(x+10)}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271228}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4ca67b8d-08c3-5756-8356-6307d581f0f1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{4}-{(x+\\frac{5}{2})}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269958} :answer-field/id #uuid "30b139f9-5928-5334-bd52-294f57457f52" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271598}] :question/id #uuid "90626d5b-7cd2-5adf-91b6-e10a0ab89eaa" :question/math-academy-id "q-140356" :question/problem "Rewrite $-({x}^{2}+5x+7)$ by completing the square." :question/worked-solution "We begin by completing the square for the expression inside the parentheses:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+5x+7\n$$\n\nFirst, we rewrite the coefficient of the linear term as a product with $2$ as a factor:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+2\\cdot \\frac{5}{2}x+7\n$$\n\nThen, we *add* and *then subtract* ${(\\frac{5}{2})}^{2},$ writing the constant term $7$ last:\n\n$$\n{{x}^{2}+2\\cdot \\frac{5}{2}x+{(\\frac{5}{2})}^{2}}_{⏟}-{(\\frac{5}{2})}^{2}+7\n$$\n\nThe first three terms form a perfect square, which we factor as follows:\n\n$$\n{(x+\\frac{5}{2})}^{2}-{(\\frac{5}{2})}^{2}+7\n$$\n\nEvaluating the last two terms, we get\n\n$$\n{(x+\\frac{5}{2})}^{2}+\\frac{3}{4}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute this result back into our original expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-({x}^{2}+5x+7) & =-({(x+\\frac{5}{2})}^{2}+\\frac{3}{4}) \\\\  & =-{(x+\\frac{5}{2})}^{2}-\\frac{3}{4} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{4}-{(x+\\frac{5}{2})}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272081 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4d854445-4b9d-5457-8fdd-3e9aafaf84c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{45}{4}-{(y-10)}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269970} {:answer/id #uuid "6c18b098-7360-5163-a283-eff16352c701" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{25}{4}-{(y-\\frac{5}{2})}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270231} {:answer/id #uuid "89f2f572-b7c1-5dea-a169-978a09aab668" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{2}+{(y-\\frac{5}{2})}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270461} {:answer/id #uuid "aa2bcef6-9c81-5bea-950e-d8b1ddb76848" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20-{(y-10)}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270787} {:answer/id #uuid "ed555ea6-dfea-51d4-876e-75d752688105" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{4}-{(y-\\frac{5}{2})}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271354}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ed555ea6-dfea-51d4-876e-75d752688105" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{4}-{(y-\\frac{5}{2})}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271354} :answer-field/id #uuid "880bee47-a8c3-50a6-937c-697f411c6825" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271749}] :question/id #uuid "afc8b4da-a3f1-5590-a7d5-e7a094b395bd" :question/math-academy-id "q-140410" :question/problem "Rewrite $-{y}^{2}+5y-5$ by completing the square." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the leading coefficient is $-1.$ So, we take out a factor of $-1$ from the entire expression:\n\n$$\n-({y}^{2}-5y+5)\n$$\n\nLet's now complete the square for the expression inside the parentheses:\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}-5y+5\n$$\n\nFirst, we rewrite the coefficient of the linear term as a product with $2$ as a factor:\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}-2\\cdot \\frac{5}{2}y+5\n$$\n\nThen, we *add* and *then subtract* ${(\\frac{5}{2})}^{2},$ writing the constant term $5$ last:\n\n$$\n{{y}^{2}-2\\cdot \\frac{5}{2}y+{(\\frac{5}{2})}^{2}}_{⏟}-{(\\frac{5}{2})}^{2}+5\n$$\n\nThe first three terms form a perfect square, which we factor as follows:\n\n$$\n{(y-\\frac{5}{2})}^{2}-{(\\frac{5}{2})}^{2}+5\n$$\n\nEvaluating the last two terms, we get\n\n$$\n{(y-\\frac{5}{2})}^{2}-\\frac{5}{4}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute this result back into our original expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{y}^{2}+5y-5 & =-({(y-\\frac{5}{2})}^{2}-\\frac{5}{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{4}-{(y-\\frac{5}{2})}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272329 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6f430bea-8bdc-5c1d-ad5c-0fb423bfc8b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{91}{4}-{(y-\\frac{11}{2})}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270254} {:answer/id #uuid "7d098b28-9b36-5a5a-a306-848196bbfbd2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}-{(y+\\frac{11}{2})}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270364} {:answer/id #uuid "c20ec7e5-a2f5-52cc-b689-4b8b3c3e13ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{91}{4}-{(y+\\frac{11}{2})}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270986} {:answer/id #uuid "f5575521-acc6-52d8-8ef0-33c9633f2919" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :a